The proposed reduction from 14 weeks to 8–9 weeks, with a possible path to 6–7 weeks, is plausible but largely asserted. The illustrative table allocates the 14 weeks into categories without evidence from the company’s actual data. This risks creating premature expectations or encouraging the organization to manage toward an arbitrary number.

